# Vault (issues + learnings)

Design detail: [vault/README.md](../vault/README.md)

## Goals

- **Practical use** — log dev/repo/skills work only; skip casual chat
- **Separate files** — daily `issues/` · daily plan `workday/` · lessons `learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm.md`
- **Obsidian** — frontmatter `tags`, topic `#hashtags`, graph color by folder

Do **not** replace `/fix-record` (long RCA after a validated fix).

## Language

| Where | Language |
|-------|----------|
| **Vault files** | Body may be Thai or English · `tags` / `skill:` / `symptoms:` / `files:` / `title:` stay **English** (search + graph) |
| **Chat to user** | Follow `bilingual-th-en.mdc` (~60% Thai) |

## Resolve vault root (before every write)

| Step | If true → vault root |
|------|----------------------|
| 1 | Read `<workspace>/.cursor/ai-skills-vault.json` → use `issuesRelative` / `learningsRelative` / `workdayRelative` |
| 2 | `<workspace>/.cursor/vault/issues/` exists | workspace via junction |
| 3 | `<workspace>/vault/issues/` | workspace root |
| 4 | Folder contains `ai-skills/` and `scripts/setup-macos-linux.sh` | agent-skills clone |

Create `issues/`, `workday/`, and `learnings/` if missing.

**WORKDAY plans** (`/workday-init`, `/workday-update`, `/workday-review`) write **`vault/workday/YYYY-MM-DD.md` only** — do **not** put WORKDAY blocks in `issues/`. Protocol: `ai-skills/workday-init/reference.md` § Persistence.

**Multi-project:** run setup with `-InstallRoot` = the folder open in Cursor → writes to `.cursor/vault/issues/` (same files as `agent-skills/vault/issues/` when linked).

## When to write — issues (no ask-first)

Write **after** finishing the user reply, **only on work turns** — **not every message**.

| Write | Skip |
|-------|------|
| code, repo, skills, git, SQL, debug, infra, vault, workflow | greetings, chitchat, trivia, weather, generic opinions unrelated to work |
| work-related skill invokes (`/debug`, `/git-push`, `/upgrade-ai`, …) | long post-mortem → `/fix-record` · lesson → `learnings/` |
| user says **save to vault** / **เก็บลง vault** | |

Do **not** default to logging every question.

## When to write — learnings (separate file)

Do **not** count chat rounds — ask whether **this topic should be findable again** (lesson, not a daily log).

Path: `vault/learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm.md` from [templates/template.learning.md](../templates/template.learning.md).

Plain Q&A → `issues/` only · **do not** copy the issues format — use the **lesson card** below.

### Both required (AND)

| # | Condition |
|---|-----------|
| A | **Closed** — `fixed` · `decided` · `wontfix` · `deferred` (with reason) — **do not** write while still investigating |
| B | **Worth reopening** — next month you would Grep `symptoms:` / `skill:` / words in **symptoms** to find this note |

### At least one (OR) — why not issues only

| # | Signal |
|---|--------|
| 1 | **Non-trivial mechanism** — root cause or workaround needs more than one line in issues |
| 2 | **Multiple approaches** — tried **≥2 distinct paths** on the same problem (commands / hypotheses / fixes), regardless of message count |
| 3 | **Repeat** — same symptom in `issues/` within ~7 days, or user says they have seen it before |
| 4 | **System friction** — git, skill, vault, Obsidian, SSH, setup likely to recur |
| 5 | **User asks** — save as lesson / save learning / remember this |

### Do not write a learning

| Case | Use instead |
|------|-------------|
| one-off knowledge Q&A (when to create issues, scores, rule explanation) | `issues/` |
| typo / single command fix, no lesson | `issues/` |
| unknown root cause / not fixed yet | wait until closed |
| long RCA after ship, ticket closure | `/fix-record` |
| casual chat | do not write |

### After writing a learning

- Same day in `issues/` (if there was a work turn) — short append that a learning was created + path
- Grep `learnings/` first — if a close match exists → **update** that file instead of duplicating (unless a different topic)

## Issues file format (daily log only)

Path: `vault/issues/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — create from [templates/template.issue.md](../templates/template.issue.md) if missing.

**Current structure (Obsidian-friendly):** each topic = `## N. title` (not one long `## Questions` section for the whole day)

```markdown
## 3. short title

#vault #git

### Question
...

### Answer / status
resolved — one line outcome
```

- Increment `N` sequentially that day
- `#topic` line under the heading: 1–3 from `vault`, `git`, `skills`, `sql`, `debug`, `research`, `ui`, `api`, `infrastructure`
- Update frontmatter `tags: [issues, …]` with the day’s topics
- **Append only** — do not delete history
- **No duplicate** same topic same day (update the existing entry)
- **No secrets**
- **Do not append** to legacy sections `## คำถาม` / `## ปัญหา` / `ประเภท:` — deprecated

## Learnings file format (lesson card — not issues)

Path: `vault/learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm.md` — from [templates/template.learning.md](../templates/template.learning.md).

**Entirely different from issues** — no daily `## N.` · no `### Question` / `### Answer`

| Section | Content |
|---------|---------|
| **Context** | work / repo / skill |
| **Symptoms** | what you observed |
| **Root cause** | mechanism |
| **Fix** | commands, files that worked |
| **When to use** | reopen this note when… |
| **Avoid** | do not repeat |
| **References** | `related_issue: YYYY-MM-DD` (optional) |

New notes should match [templates/template.learning.md](../templates/template.learning.md) (English section headings).

Required frontmatter: `tags: [learning, <skill>]`, `skill:`, `title:` (English), `time:`, `status: resolved|wontfix`  
Optional for grep: `symptoms: []`, `files: []`, `related_issue: ""`

Graph: `title:` via **Property Over File Name** — [vault/README.md](../vault/README.md).

## Search before debug / git friction

Follow [`ai-skills/vault-recall/reference.md`](../ai-skills/vault-recall/reference.md) (single source of truth). Invoke `/vault-recall` when the user wants search only; `debug` and `git-push` call the same steps inline.

## Precedence

- Vault append **once per turn** before the final reply (after main work)
- If the turn does not match Write → **do not write** and **do not** claim “logged to vault”
- If written → one line in chat: `Logged → <path>` (+ short section/topic); Thai OK per bilingual rule
